== Part 1: Proposition 6.1(a) (inputs do not depend on the answers, deterministic human) ==
200 random instances and a local search:
  largest E beta(M^(n+1)) / (L (ln(W/w(f)) + 1)/n) = 0.4087   (claim: <= 1)
  largest E beta(M^(n+1)) / (L  ln(W/w(f))/n)      = 0.4842   (above 1 would show that the '+1' is needed)
== Part 2: Proposition 6.1(b) (inputs do not depend on the answers, any human) ==
400 random instances: largest E chi(M^(n+1)) / bound = 0.3603   (claim: <= 1)
== Part 3: Proposition 6.4 (any scaffold, deterministic human) ==
250 random instances (52 with 2 B0 < 1): largest E u(M^(n+1)) / (bound of 6.4) = 0.0201   (claim: <= 1)
  largest E u(M^(n+1))/B0 = 0.3286;  largest E beta(M^(n+1))/B0 = 0.3603   (B0 = L ln(W/w(f))/n, the bound for a random round)
local search for a last round that is worse than the bound of the random round (hypotheses may be stochastic):
  target E u(M^(n+1))/B0: best value found = 0.3930  (in that instance the average over the rounds of E u is 0.5378 B0)
  target E beta(M^(n+1))/B0: best value found = 0.4952  (in that instance the average over the rounds of E u is 0.5298 B0)
